  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the monkeys behind the fence",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the scene of the monkeys behind the fence, as the meme uses the visual of the monkeys and the text to create a metaphorical comparison that the user is expected to interpret. The rhetorical question 'what's the difference between the 2?' invites the user to engage with the visual and textual material, projecting themselves into the role of the observer or participant in the implied racial comparison. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the framing of the question and the visual metaphor require the user to mentally position themselves as the one evaluating the difference, thus projecting onto the scene.",
